# The register `REG1`: the assembly and its decrement input

A register of the machine design D1 (research note `N-15`): one periodic assembly of sixteen guns
(eight blocked pairs) and fourteen reflectors serving **one** block with two inputs. Found by the
project's own search (`scripts/life_machine`, report
`notes/research/reports/R-24-register.md`, design `REG1`); the pulling and the pushing salvo
share one glider, emitted by one reflector that is fed by an OR gate.

* `reg1`: the assembly at rest, period 30 (`reg1_rest`: a reaction of 30 generations in the box
  `-347 ≤ x ≤ 128`, `-394 ≤ y ≤ 221`, returning to itself).
* `reg1DecControl`: the control glider of the decrement input. `reg1Dec_reaction` (3120
  generations, certified in 26 parts): `reg1 ∪ reg1DecControl` evolves into
  `reg1 ∪ reg1DecSalvo`, the salvo flying towards the register block, inside the box
  `-358 ≤ x ≤ 152`, `-399 ≤ y ≤ 243`.

The increment input is in `Theory/Life/Register1Inc`, the operations on the block for every
position in `Theory/Life/Register1Ops`.
-/

-- The rows of this assembly are numbers of up to 145 digits; they cannot be broken.
